==Rolling stock==

The Tedorigawa Line operates '''Type C''' rolling stock, consisting of 6-car trains approximately {{cvt|120|m|ft|0}} in length with a car width of {{cvt|2.8|m|ft|0}}. The line shares its rolling stock type with the [[Shitayanagi Line]] and [[Tozai Line (Okami)|Tozai Line]].

;Current fleet
* {{nihongo|'''6000 series'''|6000系}} — Introduced in 2020, manufactured by [[Okami Heavy Industries]]. These trains form the current backbone of the Tedorigawa Line fleet, featuring modern LED lighting, accessibility improvements, and energy-efficient propulsion systems. The 6000 series was designed for standard-gauge operation and is shared across the Type C lines.

;Legacy fleet
* {{nihongo|'''2000 series'''|2000系}} — Introduced in 1981, the same year the Tedorigawa Line opened. The 2000 series was the original rolling stock for the line and served alongside the Shitayanagi Line for nearly four decades. The fleet was refurbished in 2018 to extend its service life, but is now being progressively phased out in favor of the 6000 series. Full retirement is expected by 2027.

==Through-service==

The Tedorigawa Line does not currently operate through-service with any other railway operator. However, the line's standard gauge alignment makes it technically compatible with other Okami Metro lines, and there have been periodic proposals to introduce through-running with the [[Tozai Line (Okami)|Tozai Line]], which also uses Type C rolling stock. As of 2026, no such through-service has been implemented.

The line's extensive interchange network, with 13 transfer hubs, provides passengers with convenient connections to nearly every other line in the Okami Metro system, including the [[Nankō Port Town Line]] at Nagata-cho, which serves the port area in greater detail.

